---
title: Rhubarb Crumble
servings: 4
course: Dessert
locale: en_GB
difficulty: Easy
prep time: 20m
cook time: 40m
cuisine: British
diet: Vegetarian
tags:
- vegetarian
- dessert
- sweet
- british
---

= Preparation =

Preheat the oven to 200°C.

Grease an #ovenproof 8" x 8" dish (or half the size but deeper){}.

= Filling =

Halve the @vanilla pod{1}(or ½ tsp vanilla paste) lengthways, scrape out the seeds, and mix with the @caster sugar{75%g} and @cornflour{2%tsp}.

Cut the @rhubarb{400%g} into 3 cm pieces, halving any thicker pieces lengthways. Toss in the sugar mixture and then add to the prepared dish.

= Crumble =

Cube the @unsalted butter{100%g}{cold} and cut into the @plain flour{150%g} with a cutlery knife. Rub the butter into the flour by fingertips until the mixture resembles breadcrumbs. (Add extra flour if necessary.) Stir in the @caster sugar{50%g} and @salt{pinch}.

Tip the crumble mixture over the rhubarb without pressing down.

= Bake =

Place on a baking tray to catch any drips. Bake for 35 to ~{40%minutes}, or until golden and bubbling.

> Serve with hot vanilla custard or cold cream.